  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14173512/assets/add18e4afb099c25b56b798ac69b8b02f7cee49949ef02b5971f71ffde0d7e5c.png)\n\nCompute the measures of the shaded angles in the figure above.",
  "worked_solution": "The two angles marked in the diagram are vertical. Since vertical angles are congruent, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x-{32}^{∘} & =2x+{16}^{∘} \\\\ 4x-{32}^{∘} & ={16}^{∘} \\\\ 4x & ={48}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={12}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that we know $x={12}^{∘},$ we can substitute into one of the expressions to calculate the measure of the angles. Let's substitute into the expression $2x+{16}^{∘}:$\n\n$$\n2({12}^{∘})+{16}^{∘}={40}^{∘}\n$$\n\nTherefore, both angles have a measure of ${40}^{∘}.$",
